ng solutions for  how to function effectively through  shifting Health guidelines and how to  make plans while maintaining a loose  grip on those plans  and on the other hand there are people  like my students who've been on the  receiving end of all that passengers on  a flight where we've been building the  plane as we fly it  many of us had less than two weeks to  work out the nuts and bolts of how to  provide online learning and how to  provide services remotely that run on a  completely different Dynamic than when  they are face to face  but this is where your uniqueness comes  in  you see when it comes to people Building  Solutions and people receiving those  Solutions you are uniquely both those  groups of people  as you enter into life Post University  you will be at the Forefront of  Designing and delivering new systems for  how we live and work in this Brave New  World  and you know what it's like to live  firsthand through that turmoil you  intimately understand the benefits and  challenges of making life work in this  context in a way that I never will  you inhabit Both Worlds by virtue of  your lived experience  I said before that you all are bridge  Builders but in fact through your unique  experiences you are the bridges  so  how will you use that unique position  it's been said that the two most  important days of your life are the day  you were born  and the day you find out why  for me that second day happened here at  the University I originally set out to  become an English and history teacher  because those are the subjects that I  excelled at during school  but when I was enrolling I encountered a  professor who explained to me that there  was and remains an acute shortage of  mathematics Educators in New South Wales  and indeed across the country and most  of the western world  that day I changed my enrollment and it  sent me on an adventure that has enabled  me to achieve things I never dreamed of  and has in turn led me to stand here  before you today  now people sometimes ask me why I was so  willing to make such a snap decision to  dramatically change the course of my  life  but for me it wasn't a snap decision  you see like many of you I'm the child  of migrants who moved to this country at  Great personal cost to open up  opportunities for their children  and this is part of why I deeply feel  the Grateful burden of responsibility to  take the educational riches I have  received and use them to serve others if  the place where my service would be most  valuable was in Mass education then  actually it made intuitive sense for me  to move in that direction  and the truth is no matter how long you  have been here whether it's measured in  years Generations or millennia  everyone everyone here in this room is a  recipient of a marvelous treasure  that treasure is The Learning Journey  that you have taken through this  University which has made you a  different person to the one who first  entered this campus it's made you a  better person  now there are two approaches for how you  can use this treasure one we can use  that treasure merely for our own  advancement  or two we can use it to improve the  lives of the communities around us and  around the world now this first approach  will gratify you for a Time  but the second approach will help you  create a legacy that is bigger than you  that will Outlast you and will create  opportunities in the future for more  people just like you  the reason I've been able to do the  things I've done is because I've always  searched for ways to enrich others with  the treasure that I've received and I  hope you do the same  congratulations on all you've received  you've come an incredible distance and  overcome immense obstacles to be here  but now the real adventure begins  go and build Bridges through the work  you do  go and be bridges of using all the  knowledge and qualities that you've  developed here at the University  go and do it all in ways and places that  enrich everyone you interact with  thank you  [Applause]
 

